{{Debuffnotes
| name = Kinetic Field
| desc = {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}}<br>Immediately {{M|dispels}} the debuff and does not reapply the debuff on {{M|debuff immune}} units.<br>Hence, it does not apply the 0-damage instance to {{M|debuff immune}} units within {{M|combat log}}.
}}

 * {{Symbol|Target|Area}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Aura}}
** {{#var:Kinetic Field value4}} second after cast, Kinetic Field creates a {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} {{#var:Kinetic Field value3}}-radius negative [[aura]], Circle [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]], at centerpoint [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|21px|O]] with the following properties:
** {{Symbol|Vision|Base}}
*** Grants a 5.5-second {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} {{#var:Kinetic Field value1}}-[[vision]] radius centered at point [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|21px|O]] .
** Has the following ability formulas:
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|AuraWidth {{=}} BarrierRadius × {{#var:Kinetic Field basic1}}}}
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|Σ[[Aura]]Radius {{=}} BarrierRadius + AuraWidth}}

* {{Symbol|Movement Speed}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
** [[Movement Speed#Set Movement Speed|Sets]] ({{Code|SetMS}}) the affected units' movement speed accordingly to their proximity to the visible field barrier, upon fulfilling the following conditions:
*** Has to be {{M|Facing Angle|text=facing}} the visible barrier.
*** Has to be within the following {{Code|SetMS}} zones:
**** [[Wikipedia:Annulus_(mathematics)|Ring]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-b.png|21px|B]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|21px|Q]]
**** Ring [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|21px|P]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-b.png|21px|B]]
**** Kinetic Field checks for the unit's proximity ({{Code|d}}) from the {{Code|SetMS}} zones to centerpoint [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|21px|O]] per {{M|server tick}}.
***** {{cf|expr}}
****** {{Code|d {{=}} [[Wikipedia:Absolute value|{{!}}]] Unit-to-O Distance - {{#var:Kinetic Field value1}} [[Wikipedia:Absolute value|{{!}}]]}}
****** Does not apply the {{Code|SetMS}} component if {{Code|d {{=}} 0}} or {{Code|d ≥ {{#expr:{{#var:Kinetic Field value1}}*0.1}}}}
** Utilizes {{Code|SetMS}} to achieve the movement speed reducing effect. Hence, it affects all other movement-based mechanics.
** The {{Code|SetMS}} zones have the following properties:
*** [[File:Dota2 Disruptor Kinetic Field Radius icon.png|105px]]
**** Circle [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]] has {{#var:Kinetic Field value3}}-radius, and is the total {{M|aura}} radius.
**** [[Wikipedia:Annulus_(mathematics)|Ring]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-b.png|21px|B]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|21px|Q]] [[File:Dota2 Disruptor Kinetic Field RingBQ icon.png|84px|Outer Radius]]
***** Located at {{#expr:{{#var:Kinetic Field value3}}-({{#var:Kinetic Field value1}}*0.2)}} ‒ {{#expr:{{#var:Kinetic Field value3}}-({{#var:Kinetic Field value1}}*0.1)}}-distance from centerpoint [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|21px|O]] .
***** This is the outer radius, and applies the {{Code|[[Movement Speed#Set Movement Speed|Set]]MS}} value to enemy units [[File:Dota2 Arrow 180 Line icon.png|21px|Entering]] entering the Kinetic Field.
**** {{Symbol|fx|v}}
***** Circle [[File:Dota2 Letter-b.png|21px|B]] [[File:Dota2 Disruptor Kinetic Field CircleB icon.png|84px|Kinetic Field's Barrier]]
****** This is Kinetic Field's visible field barrier, the {{M|temporary fence}}.
**** Ring [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|21px|P]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-b.png|21px|B]] [[File:Dota2 Disruptor Kinetic Field RingPB icon.png|84px|Inner Radius]]
***** Located at {{#expr:{{#var:Kinetic Field value3}}-({{#var:Kinetic Field value1}}*0.3)}} ‒ {{#expr:{{#var:Kinetic Field value3}}-({{#var:Kinetic Field value1}}*0.2)}}-distance from centerpoint [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|21px|O]] .
***** This is the inner radius, and applies the {{Code|[[Movement Speed#Set Movement Speed|Set]]MS}} value to enemy units [[File:Dota2 Arrow 0 Line icon.png|21px|Exiting]] exiting the Kinetic Field.
*** {{cf|expr}}
**** Has the following {{Code|SetMS}} formulas:
***** {{Code|Set[[Movement Speed|MS]] {{=}} {{#var:Kinetic Field type1 value3}} , if 0 < d ≤ 5.025}}
***** {{Code|SetMS {{=}} 4d - 20 , if 5.025 < d ≤ {{#expr:{{#var:Kinetic Field value1}}*0.1}}}}

* {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|kinetic_field}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
** The debuff deals a {{#var:Kinetic Field value5}}-damage instance, in {{#var:Kinetic Field basic2}}-second intervals, to units affected by the debuff.
** Fully procs {{M|on-damage effects}}.

* {{Symbol|Forced Movement}}
** Prevents certain [[forced movement]] sources from either entering or exiting Circle [[File:Dota2 Letter-b.png|21px|B]] .
** Although the following units do not interact with abilities, they also cannot pass the barrier:
*** {{U|Phantom}}
*** {{U|Healing Ward}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Kinetic Field icon0}}
| desc = After a short formation time, creates a circular barrier of kinetic energy that enemies can't pass.
}}
* {{Symbol|fx|v}}
** Despite applying a {{#var:Kinetic Field value5}}-damage instance, Kinetic Field visually displays that it deals 1 damage within its damage interval in the {{M|combat log}}.

